%! Rules that can never fire.
%!
%! Nemo infers the types of every column from the declarations, the
%! facts and the rules. A rule whose body asks for values that a column
%! can never hold can never fire, and Nemo warns about it before
%! reasoning starts. Run the example and read the warnings.
%!
%! The example shows:
%! - how declarations type the columns of predicates,
%! - how type analysis finds rules that can never fire.

@declare person(name: string, age: int) .
@declare city(name: string, location: (int, int)) .

person("Alice", 30) .
person("Bob", 25) .
person("Charlie", 20.0) .
city("Dresden", (51, 13)) .

adult(?name) :- person(?name, ?age), ?age >= 18 .

% A name is a string and an age an integer, so no value is both:
nameAndAge(?x) :- person(?x, _), person(_, ?x) .

% A location is a pair, never a triple:
wide(?a) :- city(_, (?a, _, _)) .

@output adult, nameAndAge, wide .
